---
title: Tuscan Chicken and White Beans
course: main
cuisine: italian
servings: 5
time_active: 30
time_total: 45
leftovers: good
tags: [weeknight, one-pot]
description: Seared chicken thighs in a creamy garlic and sun-dried tomato sauce with white beans, spinach, and parmesan.
---

Pat @chicken thighs{2%lb}(boneless, skinless) dry. Season both sides with @salt{1 1/2%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, and @Italian seasoning{2%tsp}.

Heat @olive oil{2%tbsp}(or oil from the sun-dried tomato jar) in a #large skillet{} over medium-high until shimmering. Sear the thighs smooth side down without moving them until deep golden, ~{5-6%minutes}. Flip and cook ~{4%minutes} more; they won't be cooked through. Move to a plate, working in batches if they crowd.

Lower the heat to medium. Cook @yellow onion{1}(diced) in the fat with a pinch of salt until soft, ~{4-5%minutes}.

Add @garlic{6%cloves}(minced), @sun-dried tomatoes{1/2%cup}(chopped), @tomato paste{1%tbsp}, and @red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp}. Stir until fragrant and the paste darkens, ~{1-2%minutes}.

Pour in @chicken broth{1%cup} and scrape up the browned bits. Let it bubble ~{2%minutes}.

Stir in @heavy cream{3/4%cup} and @cannellini beans{2%cans}(15 oz, drained and rinsed) and bring to a gentle simmer. Nestle the chicken back in with its juices. Simmer uncovered until the sauce coats a spoon and the chicken reaches 175°F, ~{10-12%minutes}. Mash a few beans against the pan for a thicker sauce.

Turn off the heat. Stir in @baby spinach{8%oz} a handful at a time until wilted. Stir in @parmesan{1/2%cup}(finely grated) and the juice of half a @lemon{1}. Taste, adding salt or more lemon until bright. Loosen with a splash of broth if too thick.

Top with @?basil{1/4%cup}(torn) and extra parmesan. Serve with @?crusty bread{1} or over rice.

> Thighs stay juicy at 175–185°F. Reheat leftovers on the stove with a splash of broth.
